---
const faqSchema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'FAQPage',
  mainEntity: [
    {'@type': 'Question', 'name': "Which AI crawlers should I allow?", "acceptedAnswer": { '@type': 'Answer', "text": "The search-oriented ones whose citations you want: OAI-SearchBot for ChatGPT Search and PerplexityBot for Perplexity answers. Training crawlers are a separate, independent decision." } },
    {'@type': 'Question', 'name': "Does allowing AI crawlers affect SEO?", "acceptedAnswer": { '@type': 'Answer', "text": "No. AI crawler rules do not touch Googlebot or your rankings. Search visibility and AI visibility are independent switches." } },
    {'@type': 'Question', 'name': "How do I allow some AI crawlers and block others?", "acceptedAnswer": { '@type': 'Answer', "text": "One rule block per token: Disallow: / under User-agent: GPTBot blocks training while OAI-SearchBot stays allowed with no rule or an explicit Allow." } }
  ],
};
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

---
<BaseLayout
  schema={[faqSchema]}
  title="How to Allow AI Crawlers for Visibility in ChatGPT and Perplexity"
  description="How to allow AI crawlers: clean robots.txt rules that keep GPTBot, ClaudeBot, and PerplexityBot welcome while protecting private areas, plus llms.txt."
  
 breadcrumb={[["Home", "/"], ["AI Web Infrastructure", "/ai-web-infrastructure/"], ["Allow AI Crawlers"]]}>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-12">
    <nav class="mb-4 text-sm text-ink-faint" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <a href="/" class="hover:text-accent">Home</a>
       <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <a href="/ai-web-infrastructure/" class="hover:text-accent">AI Web Infrastructure</a>
       <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <span class="text-ink-dim">Allow AI Crawlers</span>
    </nav>
    <h1 class="font-display text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-ink sm:text-4xl">How to Allow AI Crawlers</h1>
    <div class="pd-answer" data-vs="answer">
      <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">
      If AI answers are becoming your discovery channel, the play is the inverse of blocking: make
      sure nothing in your robots.txt accidentally excludes the bots that fetch for ChatGPT,
      Claude, and Perplexity, then give them a clean map of your site.
    </p>
    </div>

    <h2 class="font-display mt-10 text-xl font-semibold text-ink">Allow rules per crawler</h2>
    <section class="not-prose my-4" aria-label="Reference table">
      <div class="glass rounded-2xl p-5 shadow-lg sm:p-7 overflow-x-auto">
        <table class="pdns-table" style="width:100%">
          <thead><tr><th>Crawler</th><th>Rule</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody><tr><td class="font-medium text-ink">GPTBot</td><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">Allow: / (or omit rules)</td></tr><tr><td class="font-medium text-ink">OAI-SearchBot</td><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">Allow: /</td></tr><tr><td class="font-medium text-ink">ClaudeBot</td><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">Allow: /</td></tr><tr><td class="font-medium text-ink">PerplexityBot</td><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">Allow: /</td></tr></tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </section>
<nav class="pd-toc" aria-label="On this page">
      <p class="font-mono text-[10px] uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-accent">On this page</p>
      <ul>
        <li><a href="#step-1-audit-what-your-robotstxt-actuall">Step 1: Audit what your robots.txt actually says</a></li>
        <li><a href="#step-2-explicitly-welcome-the-ai-bots-yo">Step 2: Explicitly welcome the AI bots you want</a></li>
        <li><a href="#step-3-publish-an-llmstxt">Step 3: Publish an llms.txt</a></li>
        <li><a href="#step-4-keep-the-technical-floor-solid">Step 4: Keep the technical floor solid</a></li>
        <li><a href="#related">Related</a></li>
      </ul>
    </nav>

    <div class="rich-text mt-8">
      <h2 id="step-1-audit-what-your-robotstxt-actuall">Step 1: Audit what your robots.txt actually says</h2>
      <p>
        Most sites that "can't be found in AI answers" have a wildcard
        <code>Disallow: /</code> on a staging template that shipped to production, or a CMS default
        blocking everything but a short bot allowlist. Run the
        <a href="/ai-crawler-checker/">AI Crawler Checker</a>: it shows the per-bot verdict against
        your live rules, including which bots fall through to your wildcard group.
      </p>

      <h2 id="step-2-explicitly-welcome-the-ai-bots-yo">Step 2: Explicitly welcome the AI bots you want</h2>
      <pre class="rounded-lg border border-line bg-panel-2 p-4 font-mono text-xs leading-relaxed text-accent-soft">User-agent: GPTBot
Allow: /

User-agent: OAI-SearchBot
Allow: /

User-agent: ClaudeBot
Allow: /

User-agent: PerplexityBot
Allow: /

User-agent: *
Disallow: /admin/
Disallow: /cart/</pre>
      <p>
        Explicit Allow blocks make your intent legible to both bots and future teammates, while the
        wildcard group keeps private paths out of every index.
      </p>

      <h2 id="step-3-publish-an-llmstxt">Step 3: Publish an llms.txt</h2>
      <p>
        Being allowed is table stakes; being understood is the edge. An
        <a href="/what-is-llms-txt/">llms.txt</a> file gives models a curated map of your important
        pages with one-line descriptions. Generate one in seconds with the
        <a href="/llms-txt-generator/">llms.txt generator</a>.
      </p>

      <h2 id="step-4-keep-the-technical-floor-solid">Step 4: Keep the technical floor solid</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Fast, stable pages: crawlers of every species budget their fetches.</li>
        <li>Structured data on key pages, so entities are unambiguous.</li>
        <li>Track your AI readiness over time with the <a href="/ai-readiness-checker/">AI Readiness audit</a>.</li>
      </ul>

      
<h2 id="related">Related</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><a href="/how-to-block-ai-crawlers/">How to block AI crawlers</a> (the other direction)</li>
        <li><a href="/ai-crawlers-list/">The complete AI crawler list</a></li>
        <li>Per-crawler guides: <a href="/gptbot/">GPTBot</a>, <a href="/claudebot/">ClaudeBot</a>, <a href="/google-extended/">Google-Extended</a>, <a href="/perplexitybot/">PerplexityBot</a>, <a href="/oai-searchbot/">OAI-SearchBot</a>, <a href="/ccbot/">CCBot</a>, <a href="/bytespider/">Bytespider</a></li>
        <li><a href="/ai-crawler-verification/">Verify a crawler with reverse DNS</a></li>
        <li><a href="/block-ai-crawlers-cloudflare/">Block AI crawlers with Cloudflare</a></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  <h2 class="font-display mt-10 text-xl font-semibold text-ink">Frequently asked questions</h2>
      <div class="mt-3 grid gap-3"><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">Which AI crawlers should I allow?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">The search-oriented ones whose citations you want: OAI-SearchBot for ChatGPT Search and PerplexityBot for Perplexity answers. Training crawlers are a separate, independent decision.</p></details><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">Does allowing AI crawlers affect SEO?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">No. AI crawler rules do not touch Googlebot or your rankings. Search visibility and AI visibility are independent switches.</p></details><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">How do I allow some AI crawlers and block others?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">One rule block per token: Disallow: / under User-agent: GPTBot blocks training while OAI-SearchBot stays allowed with no rule or an explicit Allow.</p></details></div>
      </div>
</BaseLayout>
